      Q. 2 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَفَرْنَقَ</span></b>  <i>He was,</i> or <i>became, bad;</i> (K, TA;)
said of a camel: (TA:) and so <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَفَرْنَقَت</span> said of a
sheep or goat (<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شَاة</span>). (Ibn-'Abbád, O, TA.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2- 
And <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أُذُنُهُ تَفَرْنَقَتْ</span> <i>His ear became raised.</i> (Ibn-
'Abbád, O, K.)

